# {{ projectName }} architecture

`create_app` is the composition root. FastAPI lifespan owns resources per worker, and the settings boundary validates enabled components. The pristine app has only liveness and readiness in an `APIRouter`. Routers, application scenarios, and adapters are added for real product operations.

{% if withPersistence %}The database dependency opens a short transaction for one HTTP request and commits or rolls back before the response is sent. Repositories and handlers do not commit. Serialize ORM data before cleanup, never share an `AsyncSession` across concurrent tasks, and keep external network calls outside a database transaction. Streaming, WebSocket, and background work require their own short sessions. Alembic contains no subject revision; use a disposable database to develop schema changes.{% else %}Persistence is disabled. No DSN, engine, session, or database readiness connection is required.{% endif %}

`PROJECT.md` and `SERVICE.md` belong to the generated application. Template updates review managed-file changes and preserve those documents, application code, settings, scopes, and migrations.
{% if withTesting %}
## 🧪 Test lifecycle

The test group supplies pytest, HTTPX, and asgi-lifespan. Build a fresh app with explicit settings inside an isolated test environment. Wrap `create_app(settings)` in `LifespanManager` before using `httpx.AsyncClient(transport=httpx.ASGITransport(app=application))`; ASGITransport alone does not start lifespan. Keep the app, client, and event loop at compatible scopes, and clear `application.dependency_overrides` in cleanup. Technical HTTP/lifecycle tests are generated; add subject tests only for real behavior.

For database integration, create a disposable database or schema/user with bounded readiness, and remove only that run's resources afterward. Do not use a live DSN or rely on one rollback to isolate DDL, multiple connections, or internal commits. A unique Compose project can provide the disposable dependency; this scaffold does not start one automatically.
{% endif %}
